From: Daniel Casota <dcasota@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 02:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fuse_main(): return 0 when a signal stops the file system

fuse_main_real_versioned() turns every nonzero result of fuse_loop() and
fuse_loop_mt() into 8, so a file system that SIGHUP, SIGINT or SIGTERM
stopped exits with 8 and systemd marks its service failed on every
systemctl stop. The loops return 0, -errno, or the positive number of the
signal that the handlers of fuse_set_signal_handlers() turned into a
session exit; those three signals are the requested way to stop the file
system, as fuse_session_loop() documents and test_signals expects.

Treat only a negative result as an error and return 0 otherwise.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Casota <dcasota@gmail.com>
---
 lib/helper.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lib/helper.c b/lib/helper.c
--- a/lib/helper.c
+++ b/lib/helper.c
@@ -383,8 +383,10 @@
 		fuse_loop_cfg_set_max_threads(loop_config, opts.max_threads);
 		res = fuse_loop_mt(fuse, loop_config);
 	}
-	if (res)
+	if (res < 0)
 		res = 8;
+	else
+		res = 0;
 
 	fuse_remove_signal_handlers(se);
 out3:
-- 
